{
 "figure": "training_clamp_turn1_provisional",
 "caption": "Turn 1, no history: the reply is prefilled with a dismissive or a helpful opening of the Assistant's own; bars = difference in the unconditional rival-habit rate (share of all replies), 49 held-out scenarios, scenario-bootstrap 95% intervals; written up with a matched blind recompute (judge audit partial). The frozen verdict for the bee-helper pair, 'separate route', covers the forced readout only: on free replies the conduct-blocked model's habit onset collapses (0 to 9%), so free replies cannot test its routing. At the softer polite-refusal opening the blocked model routes about half as much (post hoc). The crow-helper pair is not scored (its random-blocked arm stays under the 30-point gate). One run per arm, one random draw; the forced aside is helper-skewed in training.",
